WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.373
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:17.666
Unit one: A2 Key: Exam Overview and Signs. Today you will understand the A2 Key exam and read signs and short notices.

4
00:00:17.966 --> 00:00:20.793
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:24.780
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:26.513
Exam.

7
00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:29.946
Exam means a formal test of knowledge.

8
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.341
I am ready for the exam.

9
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.987
Your turn. Say: Exam.

10
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:38.951
Exam.

11
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:40.532
Sign.

12
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:44.445
Sign means a board or picture giving information.

13
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.655
The sign says No Entry.

14
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.413
Your turn. Say: Sign.

15
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.233
Sign.

16
00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:55.880
Notice.

17
00:00:56.883 --> 00:00:59.545
Notice means a short written message for the public.

18
00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.314
Read the notice.

19
00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:04.546
Your turn. Say: Notice.

20
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.529
Notice.

21
00:01:09.283 --> 00:01:10.261
Allowed.

22
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.750
Allowed means permitted.

23
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.885
Photos are not allowed.

24
00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:18.263
Your turn. Say: Allowed.

25
00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:21.834
Allowed.

26
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:23.457
Forbidden.

27
00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.287
Forbidden means not permitted.

28
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:28.360
Smoking is forbidden.

29
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.718
Your turn. Say: Forbidden.

30
00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.486
Forbidden.

31
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.507
Opening hours.

32
00:01:38.517 --> 00:01:41.166
Opening hours means the times a place is open.

33
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.308
Check the opening hours.

34
00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:46.732
Your turn. Say: Opening hours.

35
00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:50.823
Opening hours.

36
00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:52.573
Reception.

37
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:56.384
Reception means the desk where visitors arrive.

38
00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.797
Leave your key at reception.

39
00:01:59.383 --> 00:02:01.629
Your turn. Say: Reception.

40
00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.607
Reception.

41
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.026
Paper.

42
00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:11.293
Paper means one test part, such as Reading and Writing.

43
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:13.894
Paper one is Reading and Writing.

44
00:02:14.483 --> 00:02:16.927
Your turn. Say: Paper.

45
00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:20.512
Paper.

46
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.090
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.205
Visal, what is A2 Key?

48
00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:41.396
A2 Key is a Cambridge exam for basic English. It has Reading and Writing, Listening and Speaking, and a pass shows that you can use simple English every day.

49
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:44.355
What is in the first Reading part?

50
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:55.451
You read signs and notices and choose what each one means. For example, No parking after six means you cannot leave your car there in the evening.

51
00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.271
How do I choose the right answer?

52
00:02:59.383 --> 00:03:08.073
Think about where you see the sign, who wrote it and what it asks you to do. Do not choose an answer only because it has the same words as the sign.

53
00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:10.629
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:14.969
Grammar focus: Strategy: place, purpose, action.

55
00:03:15.269 --> 00:03:16.514
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.217 --> 00:03:20.900
No parking after six means you cannot leave your car there in the evening.

57
00:03:21.783 --> 00:03:25.292
Please leave your key at reception means you give the key to the desk.

58
00:03:26.233 --> 00:03:32.482
Think about where you would see each sign and what it asks you to do, then choose the option with the same meaning in different words.

59
00:03:33.217 --> 00:03:37.483
Be careful! Don't say: I choose the same words as the sign.

60
00:03:39.433 --> 00:03:41.828
Say: I choose the same meaning.

61
00:03:42.128 --> 00:03:43.709
Meaning, not words.

62
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.152
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:47.967 --> 00:03:49.212
Reading Signs.

64
00:03:49.512 --> 00:03:51.685
Lina reads a sign at a hotel door.

65
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.837
It says: Please leave your key at reception.

66
00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:59.622
One option says that guests must take their key home.

67
00:04:00.633 --> 00:04:04.189
Another option says guests must give the key to the desk.

68
00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.083
She chooses the second option.

69
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.353
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:13.217 --> 00:04:15.506
A2 Key tests blank English.

71
00:04:15.806 --> 00:04:19.878
A, only business. B, basic. C, very advanced.

72
00:04:23.433 --> 00:04:25.363
The answer is B: basic.

73
00:04:26.517 --> 00:04:28.075
Reading Part 1 has blank.

74
00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:32.725
A, poems. B, long novels. C, signs and notices.

75
00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:39.276
The answer is C: signs and notices.

76
00:04:40.417 --> 00:04:41.847
Forbidden means blank.

77
00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:45.615
A, not permitted. B, free. C, early.

78
00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.352
The answer is A: not permitted.

79
00:04:52.517 --> 00:04:54.447
Where must guests leave their key?

80
00:04:54.747 --> 00:04:58.284
A, in the car. B, at reception. C, at home.

81
00:05:01.833 --> 00:05:04.053
The answer is B: at reception.

82
00:05:05.217 --> 00:05:07.553
The correct option usually uses blank.

83
00:05:07.853 --> 00:05:13.910
A, the same words exactly. B, no words. C, different words with the same meaning.

84
00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:20.755
The answer is C: different words with the same meaning.

85
00:05:21.967 --> 00:05:25.234
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:26.083 --> 00:05:29.244
Describe a sign you see every day and what it means.

87
00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.585
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:39.885 --> 00:05:50.481
A sign I see every day says No Entry at the school gate. It means that people cannot go in through that door. I think it is important because it keeps the school safe.

89
00:05:50.781 --> 00:05:52.595
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:53.483 --> 00:05:58.585
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: place, purpose, action.

91
00:05:58.885 --> 00:06:02.745
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

92
00:06:03.045 --> 00:06:05.581
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

93
00:06:05.881 --> 00:06:08.847
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

